# PR workflow

## Branching

- Never commit or develop on `main`. All work on a feature branch → PR into `main`.
- Before calling work PR-ready, run `npm run verify` (typecheck + test + build) and report the result.

## Pull requests

- **PR title and body are written by the user.** Do not run `gh pr create` or draft PR copy unless the user provides the text or explicitly asks you to format their words.
- You may: create branch, commit, push, and tell the user verify passed.
- High-stakes changes (auth, data loss, storage, public API): also follow `.cursor/skills/old-coder/SKILL.md` evidence bar before merge.

## Extension install (local)

- No automated GitHub Release workflow. After `npm run build`, load unpacked from `apps/extension/dist` in `chrome://extensions`.
- Bump `version` in `apps/extension/manifest.json` only when the user asks (e.g. for Chrome update UX).
